<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">track</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">track</ansi> command lets you follow the trail of a
creature or player through the world. It reads the traces they left behind
and builds a map of their recent path.

Once a trail goes cold, your map will end. If your target is close enough,
an X will mark their location on your map.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Governed Skill ━━━</ansi>

The <ansi fg="skill">search</ansi> skill governs your tracking ability. With
higher <ansi fg="skill">search</ansi> skill rank, you can follow trails
farther, read more detail from tracks, and pursue more distant prey.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ The track Command ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">track <target></ansi>  Find the trail of a creature or player.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

The <ansi fg="skill">search</ansi> skill improves through use. Each time you
track, you have a small chance to deepen your mastery. As your
<ansi fg="skill">search</ansi> skill grows, you unlock new capabilities:

  Novice tracker  — See the most recent trail through a room.
  Adept tracker   — See all recent trails, not just the most recent.
  Expert tracker  — Read detailed exit information from tracks.
  Master tracker  — Your map skill shows nearby creatures and players.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help search</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help map</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">help skills</ansi>
